        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): diversify dead-provider auto-reassign instead of collapsing to one model",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter 3 timeouts from a non-Anthropic provider (deepseek/ollama/etc.), the cron auto-reassign logic silently moved every affected job onto a single hardcoded model (`anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5`). This relocates the single point of failure onto one vendor instead of actually recovering diversity — a direct regression against the operator's model-diversity requirement, and a real production risk: if Anthropic has an outage next, every previously-migrated job goes down at once instead of being spread across surviving providers.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `timer.ts`: reassignment now round-robins across a multi-vendor pool (`claude-haiku-4-5`, `gpt-5.5`, `claude-sonnet-4-6`), excluding whichever provider just died. Two jobs stuck on a dead lane land on two different surviving vendors, not one.\n- Alert log now records the actual model each job was reassigned to (previously logged the same hardcoded value regardless of what was actually assigned).\n- `launchd.ts`: unrelated but adjacent legitimate fix bundled from the same WIP branch — restart now verifies the built gateway entrypoint exists before rewriting the plist, and does `bootout` unconditionally before rebind, closing a stale-process-holds-port class of bug seen during a recent update incident.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `timer.regression.test.ts` updated to assert diversity: two dead-provider jobs land on two different pool models, not the same one (was previously asserting the single-model collapse as correct behavior — that assertion was itself the bug).\n- Full targeted suite, run locally against this exact commit after merging current `main`:\n  ```\n  ✓  cron    timer.regression.test.ts (67 tests) 998ms\n  ✓  daemon  launchd.test.ts (101 tests) 59ms\n  Test Files  2 passed (2)\n  Tests       168 passed (168)\n  ```\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean on both changed files.\n- Branch merged against latest `main` (post-merge commit `4a64802c3ee`) with no conflicts; tests re-run and still 168/168 green after the merge.\n",
        "branch": "fix/dead-provider-diversity-20260710",
